Embedded React: bake glyph sets for the European alphabets.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: bridges/quickjs/js/assets/bake-font.mjs and
bridges/quickjs/js/assets/__tests__/assets.unit.test.js. Not yet proposed
upstream.

Text an app receives at runtime (catalog titles, user names) cannot be scanned
for extraGlyphs, so a font had to list every accented letter by hand. Three
named sets join `glyphs`: 'latin-ext' (Latin-1 Supplement, Latin Extended-A,
Romanian comma-below letters, European quotes and currency signs), 'cyrillic'
(U+0400-U+045F, Ґ ґ and №) and 'european' (both, plus modern Greek with tonos
and final sigma). Each also includes the 'common' symbols.

